.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt DTFL_SCOPE_SCOPED 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_scope_scoped ,
.Nm dtfl_scope_iterative ,
.Nm dtfl_scope_region ,
.Nm dtfl_scope_worker ,
.Nm dtfl_scope_time_class ,
.Nm dtfl_scope_index ,
.Nm dtfl_scope_peers ,
.Nm dtfl_scope_addr ,
.Nm dtfl_scope_parent
.Nd nested dataflow scopes
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/timely.h
.Ft int
.Fn dtfl_scope_scoped "dtfl_scope *s" "const char *name" "const dtfl_time_class *inner" "dtfl_build_fn build" "void *ctx"
.Ft int
.Fn dtfl_scope_iterative "dtfl_scope *s" "const char *name" "dtfl_build_fn build" "void *ctx"
.Ft int
.Fn dtfl_scope_region "dtfl_scope *s" "const char *name" "dtfl_build_fn build" "void *ctx"
.Ft dtfl_worker *
.Fn dtfl_scope_worker "const dtfl_scope *s"
.Ft "const dtfl_time_class *"
.Fn dtfl_scope_time_class "const dtfl_scope *s"
.Ft size_t
.Fn dtfl_scope_index "const dtfl_scope *s"
.Ft size_t
.Fn dtfl_scope_peers "const dtfl_scope *s"
.Ft "const size_t *"
.Fn dtfl_scope_addr "const dtfl_scope *s" "size_t *len"
.Ft dtfl_scope *
.Fn dtfl_scope_parent "const dtfl_scope *s"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A scope is the context in which operators are built, passed to the
.Vt dtfl_build_fn
of
.Xr dtfl_worker_dataflow 3 .
Its timestamp class is
.Fn dtfl_scope_time_class .
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_scope_scoped
builds a child subgraph whose inner timestamp class is
.Fa inner ,
which must refine the enclosing scope's class.
It reserves a slot, calls
.Fa build
with the child scope and
.Fa ctx ,
and installs the child.
.Fn dtfl_scope_iterative
is
.Fn dtfl_scope_scoped
with
.Fa inner
equal to
.Fn Product "the outer class" "u64" ,
the usual class for a loop that counts iterations.
.Fn dtfl_scope_region
is
.Fn dtfl_scope_scoped
with the same class as the enclosing scope, a grouping boundary that
adds no timestamp coordinate.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_scope_worker
is the worker that owns the scope.
.Fn dtfl_scope_index
and
.Fn dtfl_scope_peers
forward the worker's index and peer count.
.Fn dtfl_scope_addr
returns the scope's address, an array of
.Pf * Fa len
indices from the root; the pointer is valid for the life of the scope.
.Fn dtfl_scope_parent
is the enclosing scope, or
.Dv NULL
at the root.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn dtfl_scope_scoped ,
.Fn dtfl_scope_iterative
and
.Fn dtfl_scope_region
return 0 on success or one of the errors below.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
static void inner(dtfl_scope *s, void *ctx) { /* build the loop body */ }

static void outer(dtfl_scope *s, void *ctx) {
	dtfl_scope_iterative(s, "loop", inner, ctx);
}
.Ed
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width DTFL_ERANGE
.It Bq Er DTFL_EINVAL
.Fa inner
does not refine the enclosing scope's class.
.It Bq Er DTFL_ERANGE
The product class for
.Fn dtfl_scope_iterative
would exceed the maximum timestamp depth.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_time_product 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_worker_dataflow 3 ,
.Xr dtfl 7
.Sh HISTORY
These are the C forms of timely's
.Fn Scope::scoped ,
.Fn iterative
and
.Fn region .
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
A scope exists only during the build callback that received it and
belongs to that callback's worker thread.
It must not be stored past the callback or used from another thread.
